  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "How many of these fractions are in least terms?\n\n$$\\frac{1}{200},\\frac{2}{200},\\frac{3}{200},\\ldots,\\frac{199}{200}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$80$",
      "worked": "A fraction $\\frac{a}{200}$ is in least terms exactly when $\\operatorname{GCD}(a,200)=1$. Since $200$ itself is not coprime to $200$, the required count is $\\phi(200)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}200&=2^3\\times5^2\\\\\\phi(200)&=\\phi(2^3)\\phi(5^2)\\\\\\phi(200)&=(2^3-2^2)(5^2-5)\\\\\\phi(200)&=4\\times20\\\\\\phi(200)&=80.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $80$ of the fractions are in least terms.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
